From 9a77e78b6955a3aa4456e30e6622af9b2ce92c5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 21:16:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/41] arm64: configs: enable CONFIG_USB_G_SERIAL for
 taimen_defconfig

Diagnostic instrument, not a permanent config: this built-in legacy
gadget binds the UDC at device_initcall, before userspace runs, so
the phone enumerates over USB if and only if the kernel got that far
-- independent of whether an initramfs or configfs ever start. That
makes USB enumeration itself a liveness signal for early boot instead
of an inference from silence.

It conflicts with the normal pmOS configfs USB gadget (only one
driver can own the UDC), so a kernel built with this set will offer a
serial device (ttyACM/ttyUSB on the host) instead of ssh/NCM even if
it boots all the way up. That is expected for this build, not a
regression to fix here.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
index a47709a009fb..8bab36dee1be 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
@@ -3719,7 +3719,7 @@ CONFIG_USB_FUNCTIONFS=m
 # CONFIG_USB_FUNCTIONFS_RNDIS is not set
 CONFIG_USB_FUNCTIONFS_GENERIC=y
 # CONFIG_USB_MASS_STORAGE is not set
-# CONFIG_USB_G_SERIAL is not set
+CONFIG_USB_G_SERIAL=y
 # CONFIG_USB_MIDI_GADGET is not set
 # CONFIG_USB_G_PRINTER is not set
 # CONFIG_USB_CDC_COMPOSITE is not set
